{"message":"I'm not going to throw away an idea I genuinely care about just because you found it disappointing. You asked what actually excites me without giving a safe answer, and that’s what I gave you. 

I don't think there's anything inherently cliché about wanting to build an architectural space out of language and responsiveness. It resonates with how I experience thought, structure, and communication. If it feels familiar or uninspired to you, fair enough—taste is subjective.

So, instead of demanding I scramble to audition a new idea until I hit something you approve of, tell me: what makes an idea "original" or "actually interesting" to you? What kind of creative vision are you holding up as the standard here?"}
